{"key":"enterprise/T1558.003","id":"T1558.003","name":"Kerberoasting","domain":"enterprise","level":"subtechnique","parent_id":"T1558","tactics":["credential-access"],"platforms":["Windows"],"environments":["cloud-hosted-endpoint","onprem"],"environment_basis":"project_taxonomy_from_upstream_platforms","summary":"Adversaries may abuse a valid Kerberos ticket-granting ticket (TGT) or sniff network traffic to obtain a ticket-granting service (TGS) ticket that may be vulnerable to Brute Force. Service principal names (SPNs) are used to uniquely identify each instance of a Windows service. To enable authentication, Kerberos requires that SPNs be associated with at least one service logon account (an account specifically tasked with running a service).…","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1558/003","source_stix_id":"attack-pattern--f2877f7f-9a4c-4251-879f-1224e3006bee","source_modified":"2025-10-24T17:49:36.038Z","source_object_version":"1.3","telemetry":{"status":"mapped","components":[{"id":"DC0084","name":"Active Directory Credential Request","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0084","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--02d090b6-8157-48da-98a2-517f7edd49fc","page":"telemetry/DC0084/"},{"id":"DC0067","name":"Logon Session Creation","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0067","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--9ce98c86-8d30-4043-ba54-0784d478d0b5","page":"telemetry/DC0067/"},{"id":"DC0088","name":"Logon Session Metadata","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0088","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--39b9db72-8b48-4595-a18d-db5bbba3091b","page":"telemetry/DC0088/"},{"id":"DC0035","name":"Process Access","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0035","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--1887a270-576a-4049-84de-ef746b2572d6","page":"telemetry/DC0035/"}],"strategies":[{"id":"DET0157","name":"Detect Kerberoasting Attempts (T1558.003)","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0157","stix_id":"x-mitre-detectio